  "what": "The first optimization campaign on real GPUs with real text: a smoke run (40 requests, answers capped at 128 tokens) of the publisher's command against that command with its documented speculation option, Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 on one H100 each, vLLM 0.34.0. It was stopped after the speculation setup's answer check, before the copy of the current setup was measured.",
  "not_a_result": [
    "40 requests a pass and 128-token answers: far too small to state a gain.",
    "The judge made no comparison. Every run's output throughput was empty, because the product counted only non-reasoning tokens and these answers were all reasoning (fixed after this run: internal/benchmark counts every generated token). The control's window was therefore marked invalid.",
    "No re-measurement on fresh servers happened and the copy of the current setup was not measured."
  ],
  "what_it_shows": [
    "The whole path runs on real GPUs with real text: gateway replay, planner asked on the loaded endpoint, capture, a campaign whose requests the control plane composed from the corpus, engine counters in every run, the answer check.",
    "The speculation setup drafted and accepted tokens on real prompts: 11390 of 17673 drafted tokens accepted over four passes (64.4%).",
    "Its answers matched the current setup's on all 24 prompts of the built-in answer check.",
    "About 27% of prompt tokens were served from the prefix cache in every pass of both setups, so the corpus rendering keeps the trace's shared prefixes on a real engine.",
    "On this prefill-heavy traffic the planner diagnosed time to first token and proposed bigger prompt chunks; it did not propose speculation. The harness measured the publisher's documented speculation option anyway and recorded that."
  ],
